From 69bbbe642be720da284fca93666c474acc1d2d43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:48:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] uhf: check in the generated current-version AIDL API
 dump

Adds hardware/rockchip/uhf/aidl/aidl_api/rockchip.uhf.aidl/current/,
generated by `m rockchip.uhf.aidl-update-api` now that the interface
actually compiles under --dumpapi --structured (the last several commits
in this series exist because it didn't, until now).

This directory is machine-generated, checked-in content - the AIDL-level
analog of frameworks/base/core/api/*.txt - and every file in it says so
in its own header ("THIS FILE IS IMMUTABLE. DO NOT EDIT IN ANY CASE.").
It's what `m rockchip.uhf.aidl-update-api` diffs against on every future
change to this interface, catching accidental incompatible changes the
same way frameworks/base's api-lint step does for the Java API surface.
Not committing it is what caused the build failure this whole sub-series
of commits traces back to: "API dump for the current version of AIDL
interface rockchip.uhf.aidl does not exist."

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
